From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/bridge: sec-dsim: config esc/byte clock before panel prepare

sec_mipi_dsim_bridge_atomic_enable() calls drm_panel_prepare(dsim->panel)
before sec_mipi_dsim_config_clkctrl(dsim). drm_panel_prepare() runs the
panel driver's .prepare() callback, which for command-mode-capable
panels (e.g. panel-ilitek-ili9881c.c, MIPI_DSI_MODE_LPM) sends real DCS
commands over the DSI link immediately. Those low-power-mode command
transactions need CLKCTRL_ESCCLKEN/CLKCTRL_BYTECLKEN (configured by
sec_mipi_dsim_config_clkctrl()) already enabled, but that call happens
*after* drm_panel_prepare() returns -- so every command-mode transaction
times out waiting on its own hardware tx-done completion
(sec_mipi_dsim_host_transfer()'s wait_for_completion_timeout() on
ph_tx_done/pl_tx_done), since the DSIM hardware has no clock to
complete the transfer with yet.

sec_mipi_dsim_set_standby(dsim, true) (the actual continuous
video-mode streaming enable, gating MDRESOL_MAINSTANDBY) is left where
it is -- after drm_panel_enable() -- since that's a separate concern
from the LP-mode command FIFO and is correctly deferred until the
panel has actually been initialized via DCS.

Confirmed pre-existing in NXP's own scarthgap-era (lf-6.6.y) copy of
this file too, not a wrynose regression -- it was simply never
exercised before, since the 5.5in MIPI DSI display
(imx8mp-cargt-00377-00365-glt0557201280is1) had apparently never been
booted with real hardware attached on any prior build.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/sec-dsim.c | 14 +++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/sec-dsim.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/sec-dsim.c
index 3e40f5acbc30..8511c902f662 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/sec-dsim.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/sec-dsim.c
@@ -1376,11 +1376,19 @@ static void sec_mipi_dsim_bridge_atomic_enable(struct drm_bridge *bridge,
 	/* initialize FIFO pointers */
 	sec_mipi_dsim_init_fifo_pointers(dsim);
 
-	drm_panel_prepare(dsim->panel);
-
-	/* config esc clock, byte clock and etc */
+	/*
+	 * Cargt: config esc/byte clock *before* touching the panel --
+	 * drm_panel_prepare() sends DCS commands over the DSI link in LP
+	 * mode, which needs CLKCTRL_ESCCLKEN/CLKCTRL_BYTECLKEN already
+	 * enabled. With clkctrl configured afterward (as upstream had it),
+	 * every command-mode transaction times out waiting for its own
+	 * tx-done completion, since the hardware has no clock to complete
+	 * the transfer with yet.
+	 */
 	sec_mipi_dsim_config_clkctrl(dsim);
 
+	drm_panel_prepare(dsim->panel);
+
 	drm_panel_enable(dsim->panel);
 
 	/* enable data transfer of dsim */
